{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like","id":1125140,"title":"Grimoire - What do they look like","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-05T02:02:03-07:00","id":1125140,"title":"Grimoire - What do they look like","content":"Hello there<br /> <br /> So, the mechanics for creating and using a Grimoire is pretty strait forward;<br /> * Cast Scribe Grimoire on a subject<br /> * Have the right arcana to cast it (and spend extra time)<br /> <br /> But I am about to introduce my players to Grimoires, and now those mechanics has opened up some questions for me about Grimoires since this would mean:<br /> * There is no need for any writting when creating them<br /> * Runes Isn't needed either<br /> * No need for mage sight to identify it<br /> * Don't need to know high speech to understand it<br /> <br /> With these things missing;<br /> * what does a Grimoire look like (not the subject of the spell)? <br /> * How identify something as a Grimoire? <br /> * How do a mage with to low arcanum (or wrong arcanum), see the Grimoire compared to some one who has the arcanum?<br /> <br /> Hoping to get people's take on how to do this so I can introduce it to my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T02:34:31-07:00","id":1125148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like#post1125140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* There is no need for any writting when creating them</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't precisely spell it out but the implication is that you are writing or somehow recording the Mudras for the spell. It directly mentions that the size of the recording medium as a limiting factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * what does a Grimoire look like (not the subject of the spell)? </div> </div> </div>Pretty much anything that can store information.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How identify something as a Grimoire? </div> </div> </div>It's still a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T03:38:09-07:00","id":1125161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like#post1125140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there<br /> <br /> <br /> * How do a mage with to low arcanum (or wrong arcanum), see the Grimoire compared to some one who has the arcanum?<br /> <br /> Hoping to get people's take on how to do this so I can introduce it to my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably like a very complex science/maths paper. They might know all the words involved but still have no idea what the hell is going on and cant understand it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T03:39:08-07:00","id":1125162,"title":"","content":"You do need to record the information somehow, and there's no reason you couldn't do it in High Speech if you wanted.<br /> And, if you want to, you could also add recommendations and warnings relating to the enscribed Rotes. If you enscribe Ban you could include a warning about using it for detaining people or using it for nighttime protection while you sleep without using Matter to allow air passing through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T07:37:16-07:00","id":1125208,"title":"","content":"While writing responses, I realized that I might be doing this wrong, not formulating the problem I am having.<br /> <br /> How would you in an example with setting and rules, have a player:<br /> * Reconize a Grimoire<br /> * Learn/cast from it<br /> * Scribe their own Grimoire<br /> <br /> Because I am having a hard time seeing how this is done with how the rules are.. it feels very wonky and incomplete.<br /> <br /> My biggest issue so fare I think, is the Scribe Grimoire spell. Do you cast it before or after you have written/crafted the recipient? Or do you cast it with a duration that lasts for the writting/crafting time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T07:38:33-07:00","id":1125209,"title":"","content":"There's a sourcebook from 1E, Grimoire of Grimoires, which includes a lot of examples of what they look like. Most of them are along the lines of a full book discussing the author's ideas and Obsessions and approach to magic, with a few rotes encoded throughout the text. It's often primarily a memoir or manifesto or treatise, just like any other book a person might write. Even once it's encoded, you can't just pass the rote directly into someone's mind; the reader needs to read and understand the spell and how to cast it. You're teaching the reader how to do something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T07:55:00-07:00","id":1125219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125208#post1125208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue so fare I think, is the Scribe Grimoire spell. Do you cast it before or after you have written/crafted the recipient? Or do you cast it with a duration that lasts for the writting/crafting time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting Scribe Grimoire translates a copy of a rote you know or have available to you via another grimoire into an information state on another medium and will remain in that state until the Duration expires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:08:56-07:00","id":1125227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125208#post1125208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While writing responses, I realized that I might be doing this wrong, not formulating the problem I am having.<br /> <br /> How would you in an example with setting and rules, have a player:<br /> * Reconize a Grimoire<br /> * Learn/cast from it<br /> * Scribe their own Grimoire<br /> <br /> Because I am having a hard time seeing how this is done with how the rules are.. it feels very wonky and incomplete.<br /> <br /> My biggest issue so fare I think, is the Scribe Grimoire spell. Do you cast it before or after you have written/crafted the recipient? Or do you cast it with a duration that lasts for the writting/crafting time?</div> </div> </div> </div>* Reconize a Grimoire: Pick it up and start reading it, they should recognize a rote and if there are able to cast that spell then they would be able to use that spell in the Grimoire.<br /> * Learn/cast from it: It they are able to casst that spell then they are able to use that spell from the Grimoire <br /> * Scribe their own Grimoire: The Scribe Grimoire spell will take a Rote that you know or a copy of a Rote in another Grimoire and copy it to the new Grimoire. For a +1 reach and a Mana it can be lasting (the medium that you copied it to will remain a Grimoire until dispelled).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:39:51-07:00","id":1125240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125208#post1125208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While writing responses, I realized that I might be doing this wrong, not formulating the problem I am having.<br /> <br /> How would you in an example with setting and rules, have a player:<br /> * Reconize a Grimoire<br /> * Learn/cast from it<br /> * Scribe their own Grimoire<br /> <br /> Because I am having a hard time seeing how this is done with how the rules are.. it feels very wonky and incomplete.<br /> <br /> My biggest issue so fare I think, is the Scribe Grimoire spell. Do you cast it before or after you have written/crafted the recipient? Or do you cast it with a duration that lasts for the writting/crafting time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Examples adapted from actual stuff in my home game:<br /> <br /> Samson, an Obrimos of the Free Council, has just helped his mentor clear out some ghosts from an old sanctum. His mentor rewards him by giving him a vintage pamphlet from the 60s titled <i>Invitation Transcend</i>, which is a Libertine-authored Grimoire containing the spells Know Nature (Empathy), Words of Truth (Persuasion), Stealing Fire (Larceny), and Apocalypse (Streetwise). I as the ST directly tell my player &quot;this is a 2-dot Grimoire, it contains these spells using these skills, here's a flavor handout I wrote with some excerpts from the text.&quot;<br /> <br /> The next day, Samson is going through the old sanctum with Prime+Forces Mage Sight active, looking for any leftover magical dangers. He passes a Wits+Investigation roll and finds a chest with some books. I tell him &quot;you can see under Prime Sight that one of the books has an enchantment on it.&quot; He can infer from context that it's probably a grimoire, but he wants to be sure, so I assign this Mystery an Opacity of 2 and let him Scrutinize. Surface Information: &quot;it's been enchanted with a Prime spell.&quot; Deep Information: &quot;it's a Lasting-duration Scribe Grimoire spell.&quot; I don't tell him what spells it contains. He grabs the book and takes it home.<br /> <br /> Later, during downtime, he reads the book and finds that it's a very esoteric Latin text titled <i>Ars Magica Bonisagi </i>about the nature of forms and stuff. I tell him that it's an Intelligence+Academics extended action, 1 roll per day, 20 successes needed to comprehend it. I note to myself that it's a 3-dot Grimoire containing 6 spells, and I'll reveal a spell when he hits 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, and 20 successes. If he gets an exceptional success, I'll warn him about the curse that's setting in as he reads. After his first three days of study he has 8 successes, so I tell him it contains the spells Platonic Form (Academics) and Celestial Fire (Expression), and remind him that there are others he hasn't figured out yet.<br /> <br /> Samson decides he wants to cast Stealing Fire on some Sleepers in his jam band, and he's gonna do it using the pamphlet Grimoire. He does not know the rote. He has Gnosis 3, so his usual ritual casting time is 1 hour per roll. When he casts from the Grimoire, it becomes 2 hours per roll. He does a ritual where his band plays while he reads aloud from the text and mixes it with High Speech and exhortations. He takes some penalties for spell factors and ends up rolling just 2 dice, but with the rote action quality because he cast from a Grimoire. He succeeds and the spell takes effect as normal.<br /> <br /> The Sleepers got into some trouble while under the spell's effects, and now they've been taken hostage by a local Seer. Not only that, his copy of <i>Invitation Transcend </i>was stolen. Because he didn't spend any Experiences to buy the Grimoire, it's not subject to Sanctity of Merits, so he's out of luck and he can't learn any spells or cast from it. Instead, he returns to the <i>Ars Magica Bonisagi </i>and spends 1 Experience to learn the rote Celestial Fire using Expression as the rote skill.<br /> <br /> After the whole adventure is complete, Samson's mentor asks him to scribe a copy of that handy Celestial Fire rote for the local Lorehouse. Because Samson didn't create the rote, he can only copy it from another Grimoire. I tell him that it will be an all-day Intelligence+Academics roll to copy out the relevant section of the <i>Ars Magica Bonisagi </i>to explain the rote properly. He succeeds. Now that he has a physical book describing the rote, he instant-casts Scribe Grimoire with the original book and the new book as his targets, and spends a Reach to make it Lasting. The spell succeeds, and now he has a second Grimoire containing Celestial Fire (Expression) which anyone can cast or learn from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T09:45:59-07:00","id":1125258,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Caladriu for the example. It gave me new ideas for creating different grimoires in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:25:12-07:00","id":1125326,"title":"","content":"That was a great example Caladriu.<br /> It is exactly how I would imagene studying and scribing would work in mage.<br /> <br /> Only thing that seems outside the rules is the need to research the spell, which isn't mentioned for some reason.<br /> <br /> So what I got so fare from most of the examples: <br /> * The text of the grimoire is irrelevant (you just need the arcana to understand it). <br /> * It is the Scribe Grimorie spell that actually does the scribing (no time needed to make the grimoire).<br /> <br /> So to me, the real problem seems to be the spell itself, which ruins the whole &quot;study/write arcane texts&quot;.<br /> <br /> So I don't see any reason not to scrap it and make it a roll to create a grimoire and copy it. It feels much more canon and gives a sense of having to work and study to gain knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:33:05-07:00","id":1125330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125326#post1125326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to me, the real problem seems to be the spell itself, which ruins the whole &quot;study/write arcane texts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:43:10-07:00","id":1125333,"title":"","content":"Researching spells like that isn't mentioned outright in the rules, but I sometimes like to do stuff like that to make grimoires more interesting as objects in the game world. It also might have been guarded by a jealous spirit that had to be convinced to reveal its secrets, or poisoned in some long-forgotten assassination plot, or just written clearly and easily for apprentices to learn from.<br /> <br /> I think the Scribe Grimoire spell mostly exists to explain how Grimoires come to exist in the setting. It's not something that PCs will frequently be using in most games, unless they're Masters who created their own rotes. The thing about an NPC requesting a grimoire be copied as a favor is a real thing I've done though. I also had a fun scene once where the PCs entered an Athenaeum under false pretenses and &quot;stole&quot; some grimoires by copying them, that's a good practical use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:52:24-07:00","id":1125337,"title":"","content":"I can totally see the Mysterium making grimoires out of the biggest, fanciest looking books they can find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:57:48-07:00","id":1125341,"title":"","content":"I believe you can make them out of ephemeral beings, it said something about that in the core or maybe the grimoire book. I had a copy of the Suspire encrypted into a ghost.<br /> <br /> Here we go, in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">the chapter summary for Signs of Sorcery.</a><br /> <br /> 'Chapter Four: The Wealth of Knowledge is about the vast legacy of Obsessions past a modern member of an Order inherits; rotes and advanced rotecraft, Grimoires (including Daimononika, palimpests, ephemeral Grimoires, living Grimoires and more), and soul stones'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-05-2017, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T02:15:42-07:00","id":1125522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125330#post1125330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you figure?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, this is how I feel about how the &quot;mechanics and narrative&quot; works together. Caladriu's example really helped seeing it.<br /> <br /> When I look at the rules/narrative in the book:<br /> * There is the writing and there is Scribe Grimoire.<br /> * There is no real interaction or meaning between the writing and Scribe Grimoire. It all comes down to the spell in the end.<br /> * How badly or well written the text is has no effect.<br /> * What language it is written in means nothing.<br /> * The Rote is solely created by Scribe Grimoire<br /> <br /> This doesn't fit the narrative that I want for mage. And removing the spell makes it flow much better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125333#post1125333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Researching spells like that isn't mentioned outright in the rules, but I sometimes like to do stuff like that to make grimoires more interesting as objects in the game world. It also might have been guarded by a jealous spirit that had to be convinced to reveal its secrets, or poisoned in some long-forgotten assassination plot, or just written clearly and easily for apprentices to learn from.<br /> <br /> I think the Scribe Grimoire spell mostly exists to explain how Grimoires come to exist in the setting. It's not something that PCs will frequently be using in most games, unless they're Masters who created their own rotes. The thing about an NPC requesting a grimoire be copied as a favor is a real thing I've done though. I also had a fun scene once where the PCs entered an Athenaeum under false pretenses and &quot;stole&quot; some grimoires by copying them, that's a good practical use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a need for a spell to explain how Grimoires came into existence. Why not say a archmage wrote it?<br /> <br /> And I also think it could be something that could happen allot in a game. Depending on how often the ST hands out content with Grimoires offcourse. It shouldn't however be a normal thing :P<br /> <br /> One of my players have been given a book for a week, which actually contained a couple of Rotes, but essentially, according to the rules all she needs to do to copy them is cast Scribe Grimoire.<br /> <br /> I could set it up where she has to write the text, make the research, etc.. But it still all comes down to the spell in the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125341#post1125341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe you can make them out of ephemeral beings, it said something about that in the core or maybe the grimoire book. I had a copy of the Suspire encrypted into a ghost.<br /> <br /> Here we go, in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">the chapter summary for Signs of Sorcery.</a><br /> <br /> 'Chapter Four: The Wealth of Knowledge is about the vast legacy of Obsessions past a modern member of an Order inherits; rotes and advanced rotecraft, Grimoires (including Daimononika, palimpests, ephemeral Grimoires, living Grimoires and more), and soul stones'</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like how everything can become a Grimoire (which should be possible since it is just a spell). <br /> But that would mean that no writting is needed at all. How do you write on a ghost? How can you inscribe a rune on a sympathic connection?<br /> <br /> But I am looking forward to Signs of Sorcery. It sounds like there might be allot of cleaning up in it. So I am hoping that they are gona fix the mechanics so that i follows the narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T04:26:44-07:00","id":1125535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125522#post1125522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you write on a ghost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a death 3 spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T05:24:23-07:00","id":1125552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125209#post1125209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a sourcebook from 1E, Grimoire of Grimoires, which includes a lot of examples of what they look like. Most of them are along the lines of a full book discussing the author's ideas and Obsessions and approach to magic, with a few rotes encoded throughout the text. It's often primarily a memoir or manifesto or treatise, just like any other book a person might write. Even once it's encoded, you can't just pass the rote directly into someone's mind; the reader needs to read and understand the spell and how to cast it. You're teaching the reader how to do something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should also point out that some of the entries in Grimoire of Grimoires aren't exactly what people might usually think of when envisioning a book of spells. There's an incomplete set of scrolls encoded with Arrow martial spells, of course, a &quot;cursed&quot; book of shapeshifting magic written by a Thyrsus studying werewolves, etc. The really odd and innovative stuff comes from the Free Council, naturally: the original manuscripts for a popular series of fantasy novels, the Electric Grimoire &quot;written&quot; on a spirit of electricity contained in various formats over the years, a vinyl record produced by a Satanic cabal who are also a death metal band (you have to play it backwards to hear/learn the spells).<br /> <br /> Although the strangest one in the book seems to have been made unintentionally, on a recording of an encounter with an Abyssal entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T06:18:37-07:00","id":1125570,"title":"","content":"So, once you use Scribe Grimoire and set it to Lasting...I don't see a lot of incentive for safely relinquishing it. I bet that's one of the spells that sees a lot of warping over time which leads to some of the strange texts mentioned in GoG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T07:01:08-07:00","id":1125583,"title":"","content":"If you make it lasting you don't <i>need</i> to relinquish it, You can just turn it off without undoing the spell. That's what lasting means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T07:38:39-07:00","id":1125591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125522#post1125522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* There is no real interaction or meaning between the writing and Scribe Grimoire. It all comes down to the spell in the end.<br /> * How badly or well written the text is has no effect.<br /> * What language it is written in means nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's vaguely written, but I think you're wrong on these three.<br /> <br /> The Grimoire merit specifically says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If she is capable of casting the spells <b>described</b>, she may use the Grimoire to learn those rotes with Experiences, or cast following the Grimoire\u2019s <b>instructions</b> to gain the rote quality </div> </div> </div>That implies to me that the merit assumes the mage can read and understand the text clearly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:21:28-07:00","id":1125626,"title":"","content":"Given that grimoires like the Corpus Mysteriorum contain rotes that are still being discovered, seven centuries on, it would imply comprehension is an important part of recognizing a rote.<br /> <br /> At the same time, High Speech can be overlaid onto mundane speech, which can be understood by Mages in any context, so there's no reason a Mage can't make it known by anyone. A Mage doesn't have to know the language in question to understand it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T12:17:18-07:00","id":1125663,"title":"","content":"Edit:Whoops, double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T14:00:00-07:00","id":1125686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125522#post1125522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that would mean that no writting is needed at all. How do you write on a ghost? How can you inscribe a rune on a sympathic connection?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine one way you could do it is encode some sort of reaction into the ghost so that, for instance, if someone was to hold a silver sphere to it, it would act out the rote mudra or the symbols for it would appear on the ghost's forehead or something. It doesn't seem like it would be hard to do. The ghost in our game has it written, but it's inside of him and hidden, the Suspire not being something you're supposed to copy down. So far they've managed to figure out that he is not just a normal ghost but they haven't figured out how to investigate further, or been interested in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T19:57:23-07:00","id":1125766,"title":"","content":"Personaly I think Grimorie look like this<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.egscomics.com/index.php?id=1116\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.egscomics.com/images/logo.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.egscomics.com/index.php?id=1116\" target=\"_blank\"> El Goonish Shive - 2010-07-12 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.egscomics.com/index.php?id=1116\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.egscomics.com/index.php?id=1116 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> For new readers of El Goonish Shive </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They will have a completely boring and uninteresting name on them to divert sleeper attention to them. Inside they will have an overly complicated explanation of how the spells work that is both over kill, and yet some how not enough leaving a lot up to imagination and creativity. Just looking at it a sleeper would think it's just any other book, never even a limited special edition, just another ordinary average book. Nope totally not a spell book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:23:21-07:00","id":1125896,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> <br /> That is true :P .. Completly forgot that part of Death.. Cast the spell on the pencil and you can now write on the ghost.. But the problem is still that what you write has no importance. The Rote itself is still made by Scribe Grimoire<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> <br /> I think you are right. But it is still not mentioned how this interaction is or how the text would affect the Grimoire.. Also, I think if that is how it was, a simple Knowing Prime spell would overrule the limit of the text.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> <br /> Agreed, and that is kinda what I am missing. The mechanics doesn't feel like it is supporting the idea that the mage has to research to find the Rote, or even create it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> <br /> Having the ghost act out the Rote could work as a description in some cases. But most, a Rote as I see it, is how the mage can utilize the knowledge he has in a Skill as a Yantra. So having a ghost act out a Rote that requires Academia seems odd to me.. But it is a very nice way to use for other more physical or maybe even social Rotes.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> <br /> That is exactly how I would like a Grimoire to be. Which in a sense, it can because it doesn't seem like the content of a book will affect the Grimoire at all. Michael did however point out that the description does seem to imply that the text can prevent the reader from understanding the Rote. But they have failed to explain how so fare.<br /> <br /> ====================================<br /> <br /> I am thinking of running it allot like in Caladriu's example<br /> <br /> <b>Create Grimoire</b><br /> <i>Dice Pool: </i>Intelligence + Academics<br /> <i>Target Successes:</i> Rote Dots<br /> <br /> <b>Decipher a Grimoire</b><br /> <i>Dice Pool:</i> Intelligence + Rote Skill<br /> <i>Target Successes: 10</i> +2 per Rote dot (may be higher if the creator has tried to hide the Rote)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T07:40:32-07:00","id":1125902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1125896#post1125896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true :P .. Completly forgot that part of Death.. Cast the spell on the pencil and you can now write on the ghost.. But the problem is still that what you write has no importance. The Rote itself is still made by Scribe Grimoire</div> </div> </div> </div>It has importance, because Scribe Grimoire's information still has to be comprehended to get the rotes out of it. Hiding your grimoire inside &quot;a three hundred year old ghost of your mentor's mentor&quot; is considerably more secure and harder for people to find your magical secrets in than &quot;book in your sanctum&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T00:27:28-07:00","id":1126610,"title":"","content":"That makes me imagen a mage writing pages, upon pages of nonsense in a book. Nothing to do with the spell at all.. Or maybe even just one word and casts Scribe Grimoire. <br /> <br /> He will have essentially created a useless Grimoire where nobody can learn the Rote because the text is meaningless. Or the text could be a recipie.<br /> <br /> Again, to me it doesn't seem like the two work together well at all.<br /> <br /> But the &quot;a mentor ghost containing your secrets&quot; is a very nice idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T07:57:03-07:00","id":1126707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1126610#post1126610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He will have essentially created a useless Grimoire where nobody can learn the Rote because the text is meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right for a splat whose metaphysics revolve around meaning and metaphor.<br /> <br /> One of the grimoires from Grimoire of Grimoires is an illustrated series of novels that has diagrams for its spells' mudras hidden in the pictures. That sounds both true to the description of &quot;give physical form to the mudras of a spell&quot; and within spec for &quot;a fist-sized stone can hold one or two rotes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T14:57:19-07:00","id":1126855,"title":"","content":"That is how I want to envision mage working. But the use of a spell for creating the Grimoire just doesn't work for me. And it seem like it is only me and my group that thinks so :P<br /> <br /> The example you gave is someone who wants their Rote to be understood but hidden. Maybe rolled some dice to hide it with Intelligence + Academics.<br /> <br /> I am saying, with the rules due to it being a spell, that a Grimoire could be filled with lots of content that in no way are related to the Rote. Thus, no one can understand/decipher the Rote since it seems like people agree that tou need to be able to understand the Grimoires content to get to the Rote.<br /> <br /> I cannot imagen why Scribe Grimoire is the only spell with that unique limit of text/content. There is no other spell that sais: &quot;you must have the right content, otherwise you can't cast the spell on the subect at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some spells may not have an effect on the subject depending on arcana. Using Life on a rock won't change the rock, but the rock would still have the spell and could affect lifeforms around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T15:30:28-07:00","id":1126859,"title":"","content":"If that is how you and your group see it then change it in your group, that is the best choice. It is obvious that it doesn't matter what others say that you will continue to argue that it shouldn't be that way, so make it the way you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 08-09-2017, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:48:36-07:00","id":1127115,"title":"","content":"I think you are missing something here. A book that a Mage uses to teach other Mages their Spells or Rotes isn't necessarily a Grimoire. It could just be a book of instructions in the classic wizard studying and trying to master the spell sense. A PC could study such a tome and use it as justification for spending the Experiences to learn a Rote. Or even to gain Gnosis if they are reading something truly revelatory for them.<br /> <br /> A Grimoire is a specific magic item that lets a Mage that doesn't know a Rote cast it anyway and allows them to do so with Rote Quality. It also counts as instructions like above that lets a mage learn the Rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T10:58:21-07:00","id":1127202,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> We have already changed it. Right now I am just discussing my view on, replying to the post. I am sorry if it seems like I am trying to argue (I might be mixing the two terms here).<br /> It happens with my real life group as well where a solution or similar has already been reached, but I still like to discuss it. Not so much to convince, but more just to hear others opinions on in.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1329\" data-vbnamecard=\"1329\">ElvesofZion</a> Uuh. That is a good way of looking at them. It is not &quot;THE&quot; way to teach new Rotes. It is a tool to cast magic.<br /> <br /> But I still cannot see how the text limits the spell since no other spell is limited in this way. It doesn't follow the rest of the mechanics for spellcasting.<br /> But as I said, when looking at it as a tool, I kindo want to keep it instead of scrapping, keeping that special tool for prime. Just gotta find a way to make it fit so my head can accept it :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:05:28-07:00","id":1127206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1127202#post1127202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I still cannot see how the text limits the spell since no other spell is limited in this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking about a spell in the same Arcanum as &quot;the targets can understand you as long as you're telling the truth.&quot; Prime's language-about-language shtick doesn't work so well if encoding a rote in physical media doesn't involve some degree of actually encoding the rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:34:39-07:00","id":1127244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1127202#post1127202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I still cannot see how the text limits the spell since no other spell is limited in this way. It doesn't follow the rest of the mechanics for spellcasting.<br /> But as I said, when looking at it as a tool, I kindo want to keep it instead of scrapping, keeping that special tool for prime. Just gotta find a way to make it fit so my head can accept it :P</div> </div> </div> </div>What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said. Also, no other spell contains the knowledge of a spell in it the way a Grimoire does. Other spells have their own limitations based on the way they work. Control Fire only works on fire, cause that's what it does. Scribe Grimoire requires you to encode the spell on a physical medium cause that's what it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T14:10:44-07:00","id":1127318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA pg 166</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Scribe Grimoire (Prime \u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Total Arcanum dots of all Arcana used in the spell being scribed.<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Expression, Occult<br /> By means of this spell, the mage gives physical form to the mudras of a particular Rote, creating a Grimoire (see p. 101). This spell has two slightly different, albeit related, applications: The mage may either inscribe a Rote she knows, or she may copy a Rote from another Grimoire she has on hand. Only a single Rote can be inscribed per casting of this spell, but a given Grimoire may hold multiple Rotes at a time: A large book can hold anywhere from 10\u201315 Rotes, while a fist-sized carved stone might only hold one or two, and a computer database could hold a theoretically unlimited number.<br /> When the spell\u2019s Duration expires, the inscribed Rotes fade and cannot be recovered.<br /> +1 Reach: For one point of Mana, the spell\u2019s Duration is Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As magical tools that takes the form as an object that contains information it behooves the creator to make it in a physical form that causes deciphering it to be a challenge and thus a sort of test or rite of passage and/or a piece of Equipment (CofD pg 100) in its own right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofD pg100</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Repositories: </b>Any collection of research materials and knowledge sources. A library of books, a database, and an assortment of security footage all count. A character doesn\u2019t need to build a repository to benefit from an already-existing source; this only reflects the activity of gathering materials for repeated future use. If the player purchases the Library Merit for a repository she built, the Merit stacks with the equipment bonus, to a maximum bonus of five dice.<br /> <b>Plans:</b> Characters can \u201cbuild\u201d a plan to orchestrate a complex encounter with a specific goal involving multiple people, like a heist, a raid, or a rescue. If successful, this piece of \u201cequipment\u201d grants its bonus to everyone involved, but winks out of existence as soon as the plan definitively succeeds or fails. The Storyteller shouldn\u2019t force the players to come up with every little detail of the plan \u2014abstraction is what the dice are for \u2014 though if the players are gung ho about the particulars, that\u2019s fine too.<br /> <b>Mystical Equipment: </b>Anything that carries minor supernatural potency, such as a circle of protection using salt and bone, a protective amulet, or a werewolf trap made of silver, counts as mystical equipment. For more rules about using a spirit\u2019s bane in wards and other rituals, see p. 138.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using a written Plan as a Grimoire is my favorite of those three. Of course I'd also like Scribe Grimoire to be the first Rote a Prime wielding character of mine puts into a Grimoire, because you know, it's a bit recursive and that tickles me a bit.<br /> <br /> The Equipment building rules are generous enough I'd only bother creating a Grimoire without making it Equipment if there was true haste involved.<br /> <br /> And there is plenty of elitism in Mage that making it a rite of passage to decipher it fairly common too, I'd think. I mean obsessions, hubris, arrogance, and pride are themes in this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-10-2017, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:12:49-07:00","id":1128145,"title":"","content":"<i>Right</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> Grimoires! [Mage: The Awakening] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:24:30-07:00","id":1128154,"title":"","content":"Here I was excited to start a new topic only to find I've been scooped by Dave himself! Awesome to see more previews, now it's time to voraciously devour it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:29:22-07:00","id":1128158,"title":"","content":"Really flattered that my widely acclaimed example of grimoires in play warranted a dev response. No need to thank me by name, I felt the love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:52:06-07:00","id":1128167,"title":"","content":"&quot;The sheer speed and ephemeral nature of transmitting and storing digital information plays<br /> oddly with the permanence of a rote Imago, causing some e-Grimoires (as techn\u00e9<br /> practitioners call them) to generate extraneous data by themselves, corrupt a drive into<br /> something with bizarre properties, spawn magical computer viruses, <b>or even develop<br /> rudimentary artificial personalities.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Sith Holocrons, here we go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:53:28-07:00","id":1128170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1128167#post1128167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The sheer speed and ephemeral nature of transmitting and storing digital information plays<br /> oddly with the permanence of a rote Imago, causing some e-Grimoires (as techn\u00e9<br /> practitioners call them) to generate extraneous data by themselves, corrupt a drive into<br /> something with bizarre properties, spawn magical computer viruses, <b>or even develop<br /> rudimentary artificial personalities.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Sith Holocrons, here we go!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Elsewhere in Signs of Sorcery, there's rules for absorbing a Goetic copy of a dead mage's personality from a soul stone and having them as a mentor in your Oneiros, among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:02:04-07:00","id":1128173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> +2 Reach: The mage can scribe a Grimoire into the Anima Mundi. Such Grimoires manifest<br /> not as books and scrolls, but as vast constellations of stars or rock formations. Figuring out<br /> how to read one constitutes a Mystery unto itself. </div> </div> </div>I would do this all the time for no reason other than how cool it sounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:03:24-07:00","id":1128174,"title":"","content":"If it sounds like it would be best depicted as a 70s album cover, <i>do it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:10:42-07:00","id":1128177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1128170#post1128170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elsewhere in Signs of Sorcery, there's rules for absorbing a Goetic copy of a dead mage's personality from a soul stone and having them as a mentor in your Oneiros, among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really nice. I'm looking forward to that part.<br /> <br /> I also got the idea of finding Ruins of the Time Before in the Middle East and find a whole stash of ancient Grimoires. Only problem is that these particular ruins were previously discovered and used by the mages from Kish, and every single Grimoire contains multiple Acamoth and Gulmoth via the Haunting Grimoire spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:40:06-07:00","id":1128196,"title":"","content":"Now I kinda wanna make an &quot;alloy soul&quot; nameless order that seeks Daimonomikons to get wholesome unrelated attainments in by which they flay their souls for a little bit more of a diverse attainment arsenal.<br /> <br /> Or a grand artefact that could inscribe mage sights into whole populations which could lead to mass awakenings or an abyssal incursion the likes of which the world has never seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:59:09-07:00","id":1128209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1128196#post1128196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I kinda wanna make an &quot;alloy soul&quot; nameless order that seeks Daimonomikons to get wholesome unrelated attainments in by which they flay their souls for a little bit more of a diverse attainment arsenal.<br /> <br /> Or a grand artefact that could inscribe mage sights into whole populations which could lead to mass awakenings or an abyssal incursion the likes of which the world has never seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Legacy made of Plug-and-Play souls (or Soul Stones, rather)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key"