ius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://m.popkey.co/574b46/WxVke.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: Potential things to correct:<br /> <br /> Scribe Daimonoiomikon lists Gnosis 2 as mandatory to use the spell, however considering that the spell uses Adept level practices, which require the Mage to be at least Gnosis 3 (or Gnosis 4, if you want to have two or more Arcana at an Adept level), this restriction is basically redundant.<br /> <br /> Also, considering what drawback Cognoscente gets, are you supposed to get Occultation 3 or Fame 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-13-2017, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T04:08:57-07:00","id":1128382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1128174#post1128174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it sounds like it would be best depicted as a 70s album cover, <i>do it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't run at least one game based entirely off this principle, you are missing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T07:11:29-07:00","id":1128433,"title":"","content":"Interesting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> .. Been looking forward to something like this since I started reading deeper into Grimoire's :P<br /> <br /> But in the sneak peek on p. 2 under &quot;Imbued Grimoires&quot;, it sais:<br /> <br /> &quot;By the same token, Imbuing an item that's already a Grimoire <b><u>requires extra successes</u></b> equal to the highest number of Arcana dots involved among the rotes in the Grimoire&quot;<br /> <br /> What are these successes it mentions? As fare as I know, you don't need any successes to make the Grimoire.. Just Potency and subject to cast on..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T07:14:17-07:00","id":1128435,"title":"","content":"You need successes to imbue an item, though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T03:38:01-07:00","id":1128747,"title":"","content":"Is the Potency used to determine Palimpsets twisted effect equal to full potency of Scribe Palimpset, or is it post-withstand potency? Is the &quot;twisted effect&quot; determined once after completing the palimpset and then used for every subsequent out-of-palimpset-casting, or is it determined anew for each instance of out-of-palimpset-casting? What happens when the Arcanum dots gained from Potency would go over 5? <br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> As far as I understand for now, when finalizing Palimpset, GM determines Arcanum used to create Blended Effects, and then they have to add those on each palimpset-casting using it's current effective Potency as a budget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-14-2017, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:30:13-07:00","id":1129357,"title":"","content":"Enthusiastic Creative Thaumaturgy based on pure speculation? But of course!<br /> <br /> <b>Superlative Luck (Fate Ruling) + (Spirit Weaving)</b><br /> For the Duration of this Spell, its target gains a Resonant Condition for Spirits of accidents. This takes place even when the Spell is used to place a Boon, so the target must be planning to engage in acts of sabotage, if they're not to offend the denizens of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrorize (Mind Unraveling) + (Time Patterning)</b><br /> In addition to being flooded with fear, the target also experiences a vision of a horrifying future. This Prophecy is accurate unless interfered with, and may depict anything that would terrify the target, whether related to their life or not.<br /> <br /> <b>Control Light (Forces Unveiling) + (Death Fraying)</b><br /> Light modified through this Spell has the additional effect of inflicting the Stunned Tilt on Cthonians.<br /> <br /> I've sometimes felt that Spells in Mage are rather sterile, but accepted it as a necessity of the system. Palimpsest Rotes are what I always wanted to have from Awakening, but were afraid to ask. However, if I read the preview correctly, the following Spell couldn't be produced by a Palimpsest, due to doubling down upon the same Arcanum - we'd get an extra Reach instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Purge Illness (Life Shielding) + (Life Weaving)</b><br /> Purged pathogens are vomited out by the target and upon touching inert matter are transformed into poisonous fungi for the duration of the Spell.<br /> <br /> There are also a few things I feel are ambiguous:<br /> <br /> + I assumed that each Rote has a fixed blended effect from the moment the Palimpsest is completed, as opposed to making each casting unpredictable. Am I correct?<br /> + Could a Mage benefit from Arcanum 5 blended effect, if they only have a single dot in the Rote's main Arcanum? The text suggests they can.<br /> + Could any Mage, whether a Master or not, create Rotes based on echoes from a Palimpsest? The text suggests they can.<br /> + Could Rotes with extra Reach be learned by a Mage, or do they remain a unique property of the Grimoire? The text suggests the former.<br /> <br /> I also have doubts concerning Daimonomicon as a Merit. A five-Dot Grimoire gives a character access to 10 Rotes they wouldn't otherwise have, and even when fully internalized, the Grimoire still aids spellcasting. A five-Dot Daimonomicon on the other hand doesn't grant any powers until the player spends Experiences on Attainments, and at that point the Daimonomicon becomes mostly useless to it's owner - at least from a mechanical standpoint. With Sanctity of Merits, Daimonomicon is merely a piggy bank for Experiences, with minor use as a sympathetic Yantra. Even Techn\u00e9 is only worth two Dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 08-15-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T18:34:21-07:00","id":1130073,"title":"","content":"As great as Grimoires are, my problem with them has always been using them in games. Very few times did my players decide they needed a grimoire to do something they wanted to get done. They usually were not prepared to have to go try find one, bargain for one etc to get something done, and just did whatever was needed to be done without one. I tried to insert a you need this particular &quot;grimoire&quot; to get something done story arc into my game once and it felt really tacked on and i had to come up with some really odd excuses (I think i said it was to summon a specific supernal entity) because my players were like &quot;Does it allow us to use arcana we dont have?&quot; - &quot;no&quot;-&quot;so i can cast the spell already with out it?&quot; - &quot;yes&quot; - &quot;then why do i need it?&quot;...<br /> <br /> Granted this was 1e and 2e has made them better but rote action and free reaches is probably something my players still wont consider &quot;worth&quot; the effort of trying to get. This might be worth a new thread but has anybody actually used them or do their players seek them in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-16-2017, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:18:15-07:00","id":1130085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125140-grimoire-what-do-they-look-like?p=1130073#post1130073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted this was 1e and 2e has made them better but rote action and free reaches is probably something my players still wont consider &quot;worth&quot; the effort of trying to get. This might be worth a new thread but has anybody actually used them or do their players seek them in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of making a grimoire an objective I'd make it an opportunity. In other words, they sneak into an enemy's sanctum, and just happen to stumble across a grimoire or something like that. The idea is to make it tempting enough to snatch up without it being the point of the current activity. It's similar to stealing the gems from the altar of the cult that's obviously going to hunt you down if you steal them in dnd or other treasure hunting games. Even if they don't end up stealing the grimoire, what you want is to tempt them with a choice with a sufficient up and down side to make them really pause and consider, maybe even agonize, over their course of action.<br /> <br /> If on the other hand they've been stockpiling grimoires, it paints a target on them, they have something valuable and there are Mages out there reckless enough to want it, consequences be damned. This can lend itself to ratcheting up paranoia which is also a helpful tool for pushing characters into behaving unwisely or making enemies that will provide plot fuel later on.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I typically agree, grimoires by themselves aren't really that exciting. Hence why I'd be unlikely to put a grimoire by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-16-2017, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:33:40-07:00","id":1130246,"title":"","content":"Buying one at chargen with merit dots is easy to justify. If there are rotes you want beyond than your allotted three or that you can't use yet it basically reserves them and lets you learn them later without any in-character faffing about like finding a teacher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:15:51-07:00","id":1130528,"title":"","content":"When I create an Palimpsest, who is considered to be an author of the new, Twisted Rote? Me, author of the basic-rote, or no one? <br /> This is relevant in case I spent XP to learn this new Rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}